0..78 Comment "// An eliminator that writes its answer, `if c -> C { … }` or `case e -> C {"
79..158 Comment "// … }`, answers it wherever it stands: the case is ascribed the answer, so a"
159..235 Comment "// computation a `run` binds, which states no type, synthesises it, and each"
236..281 Comment "// arm is checked against it. The rule is the"
282..352 Comment "// annotation rule of bidirectional typing (Dunfield and Krishnaswami,"
353..423 Comment "// \"Bidirectional Typing\", ACM Computing Surveys 54(5), 2021, § 3: an"
424..470 Comment "// annotated term synthesises its annotation)."
471..473 Comment "//"
474..489 Comment "// - see: #2089"
